 Mount Union is seeking a full-time Security Officer.  The Office of Campus Safety and Security employs a customer service approach and is not a police force--rather, we work closely with local law enforcement and emergency providers as needed.  This position reports directly to Director of Campus Safety & Security.  The office prides itself on working with faculty, staff, and students to provide an optimally safe and pleasant campus environment.  The department embraces the tenets of the University mission and is dedicated to helping students attain their goals related to: meaningful work, fulfilling lives, and especially responsible citizenship. Responsibilities Represent the University, Division of Student Affairs, and Office of Campus Safety & Security on campus and in the greater Alliance community. Respond to calls for assistance from various campus constituents (students, faculty, staff, visitors, etc.). Participate in processes of locking/unlocking facilities as prescribed--varies per shift. Patrol campus to ensure safety and security--and to maintain a visible presence. Serve as a parking enforcement officer--duties may include ticketing, immobilizing, and towing vehicles as needed.  Assist with parking management during major campus events. Prepare daily report/log to reflect duties and functions performed during shift. Maintain regular work hours schedule but also be available for emergency on-call purposes. Attend trainings/workshops to maintain current perspectives on matters of campus safety and security--and/or to keep pertinent certifications up to date. The security Officer must maintain the highest level of confidentiality at all times. Participates in University compliance training as communicated by the University, the Vice President of Student Affairs or the Director of Campus Safety and Security. Qualifications Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Dedicated customer-service approach and philosophy is a must! Ability to be flexible and adapt to changing circumstances. Strong organizational and analytical abilities. Valid Ohio driver's license and clean driving record--as defined by University policy. Ability to meet background check requirements--as defined by University policy. Other training/certifications that would be desired and/or helpful for the position: First aid/CPR A.L.I.C.E. C.I.T. Diversity training The specific statements shown in each section of this description are not intended to be all-inclusive.  They represent typical elements and criteria necessary to successfully perform the job.  When requested, reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions of the job. For benefit eligible positions, the University of Mount Union provides a comprehensive benefits package including, but not limited to: free tuition, generous retirement contribution, medical/RX insurance through Aetna, dental and vision insurance, and group life and disability insurance.  The University of Mount Union prides itself on its dedication to the health and well-being of its community and offers tobacco cessation resources, as all campus buildings and property are tobacco free. * Participation in most benefit programs is optional and participation is effective after the completion of the formal enrollment process and after the appropriate waiting periods.  A detailed explanation of benefits offered for this position is provided by Human Resources during on-campus interviews. Employer University of Mount Union Address 1972 Clark Ave Alliance, Ohio, 44601 Phone (330) 829-6560 Website http://www.mountunion.edu/ Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer