      "description": "Job Opportunities | Employment Opportunities For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Assistant Professor, Biochemistry & Chemistry | Employment Opportunities  page has loaded. Assistant Professor, Biochemistry & Chemistry | Employment Opportunities  page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Job Opportunities Menu Job Opportunities Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. Employment Opportunities powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Assistant Professor, Biochemistry & Chemistry Print Apply ﻿ Assistant Professor, Biochemistry & Chemistry Location 1972 Clark Ave, Alliance, OH Job Type Faculty - Full Time Job Number 2025-00606 Department Academic Affairs Division Faculty Opening Date 08/28/2026 Description Benefits Description The department of Biochemistry, Chemistry, and Physics at the University of Mount Union, an ACS approved program, invites applicants for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Chemistry and biochemistry position to begin August 1, 2027.  Our department of eleven faculty members strives for excellence in student learning through interactions in the classroom, working together in teaching labs, and undergraduate research experiences. Responsibilities Teaching responsibilities may include courses in general chemistry, organic chemistry, polymer chemistry, and biochemistry.  Development of a strong undergraduate research program is required. Qualifications Applicants should hold a Ph.D. in Chemistry or Biochemistry; ABD will be considered.  Applicants should submit a letter of interest, curriculum vitae, teaching philosophy and statement of research interests to www.mountunion.edu/employment .  Three letters of recommendation will be requested of applicants after the initial review. Please contact the search committee chair, Dr. Scott Mason, masonss@mountunion.edu , with any questions.  Review of applications will begin September 18, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Descriptive Information The University of Mount Union is an equal opportunity employer. The University of Mount Union prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, gender, gender identity or expression, sex, sexual orientation, religion, age, color, creed, national or ethnic origin, veteran status, marital or parental status, pregnancy, disability, or genetic information in student admissions, ?nancial aid, educational or athletic programs, or employment as now or may hereafter be required by University policy and federal or state law. The University of Mount Union, a private Midwestern institution founded in 1846, o?ers a rigorous and relevant academic program that is grounded in the liberal arts tradition. Mount Union’s more than 2,300 students can select from 56 broad-based and career speci?c undergraduate majors as well as master’s programs in physician assistant studies and education and a doctoral program in physical therapy. Known for its academic excellence and personal approach, the institution boasts a 13:1 student-faculty ratio and a curriculum delivered by dedicated faculty members, 87% of whom hold terminal degrees in their ?elds. Since 2005, nearly $110 million has been invested in the construction and renovation of modern facilities including a recreation center, apartment-style housing options, health, and medical sciences facility, and performing arts center. Primarily residential in nature, Mount Union’s picturesque 123-acre campus is located in Alliance, OH (Population23,000), within 80 miles of both Cleveland and Pittsburgh. The 162-acre Huston-Brumbaugh Nature Center is located six miles away. The University’s endowment is in excess of $141 million. The University strives to make its exceptional educational experience accessible to students of all ?nancial backgrounds. Its increasingly diverse campus community bene?ts from a student-centered approach and array of activities for cultural, civic, and social development. Students experience outstanding opportunities for success after graduation, both in the workforce and in graduate study. For more information, visit w ww.mountunion.edu For benefit eligible positions, the University of Mount Union provides a comprehensive benefits package including, but not limited to: free tuition, generous retirement contribution, medical/RX insurance through Aetna, dental and vision insurance, and group life and disability insurance.  The University of Mount Union prides itself on its dedication to the health and well-being of its community and offers tobacco cessation resources, as all campus buildings and property are tobacco free. * Participation in most benefit programs is optional and participation is effective after the completion of the formal enrollment process and after the appropriate waiting periods.  A detailed explanation of benefits offered for this position is provided by Human Resources during on-campus interviews. Employer University of Mount Union Address 1972 Clark Ave Alliance, Ohio, 44601 Phone (330) 829-6560 Website http://www.mountunion.edu/ Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the ex